<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Trianon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Trianon was the peace treaty signed on 4 June 1920 at the Grand Trianon palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> between the Allied powers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It cut Hungary's territory by about two-thirds, transferring lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>, the Kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, and left millions of Hungarians outside the new borders. Its revision became the central aim of interwar Hungarian politics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-trianon.jpg" alt="Treaty of Trianon" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agence Rol · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Signature_de_la_Paix_avec_la_Hongrie,_en_t%C3%AAte_Ben%C3%A1rd_%C3%81gost_hongrois(passant_devant_un_piquet_d%27honneur_%C3%A0_Versailles).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
